   "evidence": "Exact rest-frame kinematics with P = (M,0,0,0), q = (q\u2070,0,0,q\u00b3), elastic P'\u00b2 = P\u00b2 = M\u00b2 gives 2P\u00b7\u0394 = t, hence \u0394\u2070 = t/(2M), |\u0394\u20d7|\u00b2 = t\u00b2/(4M\u00b2) - t, and with \u03be = \u0394\u00b7q/P\u00b7q and v = q\u00b3/q\u2070 the physical condition is (\u03c4/2 - \u03be)\u00b2/v\u00b2 \u2264 \u03c4\u00b2/4 - \u03c4 for \u03c4 = t/M\u00b2. At v = 1 this is exactly \u03c4 \u2264 -\u03be\u00b2/(1-\u03be); for v\u00b2 = 1+\u03b5 the max of \u03c4 is -\u03be\u00b2/(1-\u03be) + \u03b5[\u03be\u00b2/(1-\u03be)\u00b2 + \u03be\u2074/(4(1-\u03be)\u00b3)] + O(\u03b5\u00b2) with \u03b5 = Q\u00b2M\u00b2/(P\u00b7q)\u00b2. Numerically, M = 1, \u03be = 0.1, v\u00b2 = 2: exact boundary \u03c4 = -0.00526 versus the formula's -0.01111 \u2014 a factor of two, not a rounding difference.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics.lean",
   "fix": "Say in the docstring that `xi` is the light-cone momentum-loss fraction, which agrees with `Invariants.xi` only up to relative corrections of order `Q\u00b2M\u00b2/(P\u00b7q)\u00b2` (exactly in the Bjorken limit), and drop the unqualified claim that the target-elastic region is `t \u2264 tMinElastic M Invariants.xi`. The roadmap's Layer 0.2 wording carries the same imprecision, so flag it to the humans rather than restating it here as exact.",
   "issue": "The docstring explicitly identifies the argument `xi` with the invariant `Invariants.xi = \u0394\u00b7q/P\u00b7q` and then asserts, as exact two-body threshold kinematics, that the accessible region is `t \u2264 tMinElastic M \u03be`, i.e. `|t| \u2265 \u03be\u00b2M\u00b2/(1-\u03be)`. The formula `-\u03be\u00b2M\u00b2/(1-\u03be)` is exact in the light-cone momentum-loss fraction `\u03be_LC = \u0394\u207a/P\u207a` (equivalently in the skewness, via `\u03be_LC = 2\u03b7/(1+\u03b7)` and `t_min = -4M\u00b2\u03b7\u00b2/(1-\u03b7\u00b2)`), not in `\u0394\u00b7q/P\u00b7q`; the two coincide only as `Q\u00b2M\u00b2/(P\u00b7q)\u00b2 \u2192 0`. No theorem in the file makes this claim, so nothing proved is false, but the prose is the interface a later theorem will be stated against.",
   "line": "215"
  }
